---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Senior Dog Care Checklist: Everything Your Aging Dog Needs";
const description = "A complete senior dog care checklist covering vet visits, nutrition, exercise, joint health, dental care, and home adjustments — everything you need to keep your older dog comfortable and healthy.";
const date = "2026-06-25";
const siteUrl = "https://www.petaginghub.com";
const canonicalPath = "/en/blog/senior-dog-care-checklist/";
const canonicalURL = new URL(canonicalPath, siteUrl);

const hrefLangAlternates = [
{ lang: 'en', url: siteUrl + '/en/blog/senior-dog-care-checklist/' },
{ lang: 'x-default', url: siteUrl + '/en/blog/senior-dog-care-checklist/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
title={title}
description={description}
breadcrumbs={[
{ label: 'Blog', url: '/en/blog/' },
{ label: 'Senior Dog Care Checklist', url: canonicalURL.pathname }
]}
lang="en"
hrefLangAlternates={hrefLangAlternates}>

<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-10 px-4">
<header class="mb-8">
<span class="inline-block bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-4">Dogs</span>
<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4">{title}</h1>
<p class="text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Your dog just slowed down a little. Here's what to actually do about it — a practical checklist for recording observations and discussing individual care with a veterinarian; it is not a validated health score.</p>
</header>

<div class="space-y-10">

<section>
<h2>When Does a Dog Become "Senior"?</h2>
<p>There's no single age — it depends heavily on size. The table below is an existing site reference, not veterinary cutoffs, a validated lifespan forecast or a feeding prescription. Individual care needs vary:</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mt-3">
<table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
<thead>
<tr class="bg-slate-100">
<th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-bold text-slate-700">Breed Size</th>
<th class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-slate-700 text-center">Senior Age</th>
<th class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-slate-700 text-center">Avg. Lifespan</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{[
["Small (&lt;20 lbs)", "10–11 years", "12–16 years"],
["Medium (20–50 lbs)", "8–9 years", "10–14 years"],
["Large (50–90 lbs)", "7–8 years", "9–13 years"],
["Giant (&gt;90 lbs)", "5–6 years", "7–10 years"],
].map(([size, age, lifespan], i) => (
<tr class={i % 2 === 0 ? "bg-white" : "bg-slate-50"}>
<td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-800" set:html={size}></td>
<td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-slate-700">{age}</td>
<td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-slate-700">{lifespan}</td>
</tr>
))}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 text-sm">Once your dog enters the senior stage, the right routines matter enormously. Our <a href="/en/blog/senior-dog-care/" class="text-blue-600 underline">senior dog care guide</a> covers the full picture of what to adjust and when.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>✅ Veterinary Care Checklist</h2>
<div class="space-y-3">
{[
{ item: "Discuss an individual examination and testing plan", detail: "Age-related conditions like kidney disease and hypothyroidism often show up in bloodwork before symptoms appear." },
{ item: "Discuss whether laboratory testing is appropriate", detail: "Ask which tests and intervals fit the dog’s history, findings and risks; no single panel applies automatically to every dog above one age." },
{ item: "Get a dental cleaning if overdue", detail: "Oral problems can cause pain even when a dog still eats; assessment and procedure timing depend on individual findings." },
{ item: "Discuss a pain assessment for arthritis", detail: "Record stiffness, limping or changes in daily function; these observations require assessment, not a diagnosis from a prevalence figure." },
{ item: "Update parasite prevention year-round", detail: "Senior dogs have less immune resilience. Don't skip heartworm, flea, and tick prevention in winter." },
{ item: "Ask about a blood pressure check", detail: "Hypertension is underdiagnosed in older dogs. It can cause sudden blindness or stroke if uncontrolled." },
].map(({ item, detail }) => (
<div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
<span class="text-green-500 font-bold mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>
<div>
<p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm">{item}</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1">{detail}</p>
</div>
</div>
))}
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>✅ Nutrition Checklist</h2>
<div class="bg-amber-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-amber-100">
<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 text-sm">
<li>Choose a complete and balanced diet appropriate to the species and life stage. Review body condition, muscle condition, weight trend, appetite, activity and medical history with your veterinarian. Age alone does not prescribe a calorie cut, fixed protein percentage or low-phosphorus diet.</li>
<li>Supplements are not automatically needed with a complete and balanced diet. Benefits, contraindications and interactions depend on the product, species and condition. Discuss them with your veterinarian; this page does not provide a dose or promise effectiveness.</li>
<li><strong>Watch for weight gain:</strong> Obesity worsens arthritis, heart disease, and diabetes. Review body condition, weight trend, current portions, treats and the feeding plan with your veterinarian rather than changing portions by a single observation.</li>
<li><strong>Watch for weight loss too:</strong> Unexplained weight loss in seniors can signal kidney disease, diabetes, cancer, or dental pain making eating difficult.</li>
<li><strong>Keep fresh water available always:</strong> Senior dogs are more prone to dehydration and kidney strain. Consider a pet water fountain to encourage drinking.</li>
<li>Review portions and meal patterns with your veterinarian based on appetite, nutrition and tolerance—not a universal meal count.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 text-sm">For a full breakdown of how calorie, protein, and supplement needs shift across a dog's life, see our <a href="/en/blog/pet-nutrition-by-age/" class="text-blue-600 underline">pet nutrition by life stage guide</a>.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>✅ Exercise &amp; Mobility Checklist</h2>
<div class="space-y-3">
{[
{ item: "Shorter, more frequent walks instead of one long one", detail: "Some dogs may suit shorter, gentler activity. Adapt it to fitness, health and response; do not force movement through pain or marked fatigue." },
{ item: "Let your dog set the pace", detail: "Forcing a senior dog to keep up on a run or long hike can injure joints that are already compromised." },
{ item: "Add swimming or hydrotherapy if available", detail: "Swimming or rehabilitation may not suit every dog; ask your veterinarian whether it is appropriate for the condition and individual response." },
{ item: "Use ramps or steps for furniture and car access", detail: "Jumping on/off couches and in/out of cars is a major source of spinal and joint injury in senior dogs." },
{ item: "Place non-slip mats on slick floors", detail: "Hardwood and tile floors are hard to navigate with weakened hindquarters. Yoga mats work well." },
{ item: "Keep up with gentle daily movement", detail: "Adapt movement and rest to the dog’s condition, comfort and response, with veterinary guidance for mobility problems." },
].map(({ item, detail }) => (
<div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
<span class="text-green-500 font-bold mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>
<div>
<p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm">{item}</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1">{detail}</p>
</div>
</div>
))}
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>✅ Home Environment Checklist</h2>
<div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-slate-200">
<ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 text-sm">
<li><strong>Orthopedic dog bed:</strong> Memory foam reduces pressure on arthritic joints. Place in a warm, draft-free spot. Monitor changes from the dog’s own sleep and activity pattern.</li>
<li>Discuss eating posture and accessible feeding arrangements if your dog has discomfort; do not automatically raise every dog’s bowls.</li>
<li><strong>More frequent potty breaks:</strong> Adapt access and opportunities to individual needs. Urinary incontinence is common and manageable — don't punish accidents.</li>
<li><strong>Nightlights for dogs with failing vision:</strong> Senior dogs often develop cataracts or nuclear sclerosis. A small nightlight helps them navigate at night.</li>
<li><strong>Keep the layout consistent:</strong> Dogs with cognitive decline rely heavily on spatial memory. Rearranging furniture can cause significant confusion and anxiety.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>✅ Mental Health &amp; Enrichment Checklist</h2>
<div class="space-y-3">
{[
{ item: "Maintain consistent daily routines", detail: "Same walk times, mealtimes, and bedtime reduce anxiety — especially important for dogs showing cognitive changes." },
{ item: "Offer sniff walks (let them smell everything)", detail: "Mental stimulation from sniffing is tiring in a good way. Offer sniffing opportunities suited to your dog’s comfort and interests; no fixed exercise equivalence is assumed." },
{ item: "Gentle training sessions", detail: "Short, positive-reinforcement training keeps minds sharp and reinforces your bond. Adapt the session to comfort, attention and response." },
{ item: "Watch for CCD signs", detail: "Canine Cognitive Dysfunction signs include: staring at walls, getting 'stuck' in corners, waking at night, forgetting housetraining. Ask your vet about medications that can help." },
{ item: "Maximize quality time", detail: "Quiet companionship — sitting together, gentle petting, calm car rides — matters enormously to senior dogs." },
].map(({ item, detail }) => (
<div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
<span class="text-green-500 font-bold mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>
<div>
<p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm">{item}</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1">{detail}</p>
</div>
</div>
))}
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Warning Signs: When to Call the Vet</h2>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-3">Learning to recognize <a href="/en/blog/dog-aging-signs/" class="text-blue-600 underline">the early signs of aging in dogs</a> before they become emergencies can make a real difference in outcomes.</p>
<div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-5">
<p class="font-semibold text-red-800 text-sm mb-3">For collapse, labored breathing or an obvious emergency, seek veterinary help immediately. Contact your veterinarian promptly about other new or persistent changes, including:</p>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-red-700 text-sm list-disc pl-4">
<li>Sudden collapse or inability to stand</li>
<li>Rapid, labored, or noisy breathing</li>
<li>Sudden vision loss (bumping into things)</li>
<li>Drinking or urinating dramatically more or less than usual</li>
<li>Unexplained weight loss or a changing trend</li>
<li>Lumps that appear or change size rapidly</li>
<li>Not eating or a marked appetite change — contact a veterinarian promptly</li>
<li>Sudden behavioral changes — confusion, aggression, extreme clinginess</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="space-y-4">
{[
{ q: "How often should a senior dog see the vet?", a: "Discuss an individual examination and testing plan with your veterinarian. Age, history, examination findings and risk factors guide the schedule and tests." },
{ q: "What is the best food for senior dogs?", a: "Choose a complete and balanced diet appropriate to the species and life stage. Review body condition, muscle condition, weight trend, appetite, activity and medical history with your veterinarian. Age alone does not prescribe a calorie cut, fixed protein percentage or low-phosphorus diet." },
{ q: "Should I give my senior dog supplements?", a: "Supplements are not automatically needed with a complete and balanced diet. Benefits, contraindications and interactions depend on the product, species and condition. Discuss them with your veterinarian; this page does not provide a dose or promise effectiveness." },
{ q: "My old dog sleeps all day — is that normal?", a: "Compare sleep and activity with your dog’s usual pattern. New, persistent or worsening changes warrant veterinary discussion; a sleep-hour count cannot rule out pain or illness." },
].map(({ q, a }) => (
<details class="group border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
<summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer px-5 py-4 bg-white hover:bg-slate-50 font-medium text-slate-800">
{q}
<span class="ml-4 text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
</summary>
<div class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600 text-sm bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-100">{a}</div>
</details>
))}
</div>
</section>

</div>

<div class="mt-8 bg-amber-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-amber-100 text-center">
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm mb-3">Find out your dog's age in human years — by breed size.</p>
<a href="/en/tools/dog-age-calculator/" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-amber-500 hover:bg-amber-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Try our Dog Age Calculator →</a>
</div>
<div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
<a href="/en/tools/dog-age-calculator/" class="px-5 py-3 bg-amber-500 hover:bg-amber-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Dog Age Calculator</a>
<a href="/en/blog/dog-human-years/" class="px-5 py-3 bg-slate-100 hover:bg-slate-200 text-slate-800 font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Dog Age in Human Years →</a>
</div>

<footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 text-sm text-slate-400">
<p>Last updated: {date}</p>
<p class="mt-2">Disclaimer: This content is for general informational purposes only and does not constitute veterinary advice. Consult your veterinarian for guidance specific to your pet.</p>
</footer>
</article>

<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-600">Sources: <a href="https://www.aaha.org/resources/2023-aaha-senior-care-guidelines-for-dogs-and-cats/nutrition/">AAHA individualized nutrition</a>; <a href="https://www.aaha.org/resources/2023-aaha-senior-care-guidelines-for-dogs-and-cats/pain-management/">AAHA pain care</a>; <a href="https://www.vet.cornell.edu/hospitals/services/emergency-and-critical-care-0">Cornell emergency signs</a>. These do not validate the legacy lifespan table or a fixed feeding or exercise prescription.</p>
